---
import Section from './Section.astro';

const spec = [
  {
    term: 'Shipped as',
    detail:
      'A component your team adds to the build it already ships, with a C interface at its edge. There is nothing to port and no platform to stand up.',
  },
  {
    term: 'Self-contained',
    detail:
      'One component carries the record, how it is stored, and how it answers multi-dimensional questions.',
  },
  {
    term: 'Answers',
    detail:
      'Multi-dimensional questions about what happened and why, on the device, from the record it keeps.',
  },
  {
    term: 'Travels',
    detail:
      'A record written on one machine reads on another, with no conversion step and no export.',
  },
  {
    term: 'Reaches',
    detail:
      'One codebase spans your product line, from the smallest target to the largest, so the record format does not change with the hardware.',
  },
  {
    term: 'The boundary',
    detail:
      'The record format and the research are public, so a second implementation can recompute an address. The engine, the device kernels, and the conformance program are the commercial layer.',
  },
];
---

<Section
  id="product"
  label="Product"
  title="Runs inside the product you already ship"
  lede="Your team adds Ktema to the build it already has, and the product can answer multi-dimensional questions from its own record."
>
  <dl class="spec">
    {
      spec.map((row) => (
        <>
          <dt>{row.term}</dt>
          <dd>{row.detail}</dd>
        </>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <p class="note">
    The record is also the evidence a regulated product needs. The CRA reporting duty has applied
    since 11 September 2026, and its main obligations arrive in December 2027. The EU AI Act asks
    for logging over the life of a high-risk system.
  </p>

</Section>

<style>
  .link-row {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
